<BaseLayout title="A Difficult Habit to Break — Racquet Habit" description="Court Note 001 from Racquet Habit, a society of repeat players established in Yerevan in 2026.">
  <section class="editorial-hero editorial-hero--journal">
    <span class="eyebrow">Court Note 001 · Two-minute read</span>
    <h1>A difficult habit to <em>break.</em></h1>
    <p>There is always time for another set. At least that is the working theory.</p>
  </section>
  <section class="editorial-body">
    <aside class="editorial-aside"><span>Journal no. 001</span><span>Yerevan / July 2026</span><span>Filed after court hours</span></aside>
    <article class="editorial-copy">
      <p>The court is a rectangle. The habit is not nearly so contained.</p>
      <h2>We know the pattern.</h2>
      <p>It starts with one booking. Then another racquet, a preferred grip, a particular warm-up, a weather app checked with unreasonable frequency. Weekends become draw sheets. Friends become opponents. The final set develops sequels.</p>
      <p>Racquet Habit exists for the space between sport and daily life—for people who do not need encouragement to play, only better things to carry with them.</p>
      <h2>Our uniform is deliberately composed.</h2>
      <p>No loud performance slogans. No borrowed club crest. No claim that every point is a metaphor for greatness. We prefer useful materials, exact typography and visual devices built from the game itself.</p>
      <div class="principles">
        <div><h3>Play often.</h3><p>Court hours are never quite over.</p></div>
        <div><h3>Choose precisely.</h3><p>Fewer pieces, better considered, used until they acquire their own record.</p></div>
        <div><h3>Leave room for another.</h3><p>Because the last set is almost always a myth.</p></div>
      </div>
      <a class="button button--red" href="/shop">Shop Collection 01 <span>↗</span></a>
    </article>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
